{"step_index":151,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:44:22Z","content":"All three issues have been completely fixed!\n\nHere is what was fixed and how it works:\n\n---\n\n### What Changed:\n\n1. **Stays Unlocked for the Entire Browser Session**:\n   - The extension now uses in-memory browser session storage (`chrome.storage.session`).\n   - You only enter your master password **once**. \n   - Refreshing a tab, switching tabs, or navigating to other websites **will no longer ask for the master password again**.\n   - It stays unlocked until you **close the browser** or click the **`🔒 Lock`** button!\n\n2. **Saved Passwords Never Disappear on Refresh**:\n   - The background worker now retains the active session key across refreshes so your saved passwords stay visible and ready for auto-fill.\n\n3. **Unified Vault (No More Duplicate Saving between Localhost & Extension)**:\n   - Added a **Full-Screen Dashboard (`vault.html`)** directly inside the extension!\n   - Click the **`🖥️`** icon at the top of the extension popup to open the full dashboard in a tab.\n   - Anything you save in the full dashboard is **instantly available for auto-fill in the extension**, and vice-versa!\n   - There is also an **\"📂 Import Localhost Backup\"** button in the dashboard if you want to import your existing passwords from the localhost web app in 1 click.\n\n4. **Smart Subdomain & Brand Matching (NeoCollab & Examly)**:\n   - The auto-fill matcher now recognizes subdomains like `vitvellore312.examly.io` matching `examly.io`, and `neocollab` matching `app.neocollab.com`.\n\n---\n\n### How to Apply the Update (Takes 5 seconds):\n\n1. Go to your extensions tab:\n   - Chrome: `chrome://extensions`\n   - Edge: `edge://extensions`\n2. Find **Offline Vault - Password Manager**.\n3. Click the **Reload / Refresh icon (🔄)** on its card.\n\nNow refresh **NeoCollab** or **Examly** — unlock once, and it will stay unlocked and ready to auto-fill without asking again!","thinking":"**Fixing Frequent Password Prompts**\n\nThe master password prompt appearing on every refresh was addressed using in-memory session persistence. Caching the derived encryption key within the browser session via a specific storage mechanism prevents repeated prompts. This mechanism ensures the key persists across tabs, refreshes, and popup reopens within the same browser session.\n\n\n"}
