{"step_index":153,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:51:00Z","content":"Here is why this happened:\n\n* **Image 1** is your **Localhost Webpage** (stored in the webpage's local IndexedDB).\n* **Image 2** is your **Browser Extension** (stored in Chrome's extension storage).\n\nBecause web browsers keep webpage data isolated from browser extension data for security, the extension doesn't have your passwords yet.\n\n---\n\n### How to transfer your passwords to the extension (Takes 15 seconds):\n\n#### Step 1: Export from the Webpage\n1. Go back to your **localhost webpage tab** (Image 1).\n2. Click the **Settings gear icon (⚙️)** at the top right.\n3. Click **\"Export Backup (.json)\"** to download your vault backup file to your computer.\n\n#### Step 2: Import into the Extension\n1. Click the **🛡️ Offline Vault** extension icon in your toolbar.\n2. Look at the top bar of the popup (in your Image 2) and click the **Computer Monitor icon (`🖥️`)** next to the title.\n   - This opens the **Unified Extension Dashboard** in a full tab!\n3. Click the button: **\"📂 Import Localhost Backup\"**.\n4. Select the `.json` file you just downloaded and enter your master password.\n\n**Done!** Both **`neocollab`** and **`github`** will now be permanently inside your extension!\n\n---\n\n### Alternative: Add directly in the extension\nIn your Image 2, you can also just click the green **`＋ Add`** button in the popup:\n- Enter your email `vijay.rohra2025@vitstudent...` and password.\n- Click **Save Encrypted**.\n\nOnce saved in the extension, refreshing Examly/NeoCollab will immediately show your credentials and the **`⚡ Auto-Fill`** button!","thinking":"**Interpreting Password Manager Snapshot**\n\nThe user is interacting with an offline password manager application, evident from the \"Strictly Local Storage\" banner.  Observed entries include credentials for \"neocollab\" and \"github.\"  The application appears to be running locally via `localhost` or a `file://` scheme.\n\n\n**Isolating Storage Discrepancy**\n\nThe password manager stores data locally within the webpage's IndexedDB, separate from the extension's storage. The extension's storage is empty. The extension's lack of passwords is due to the user saving credentials within the web application.\n\nA direct data migration path between the two storage locations is needed. Exporting the data from the web application and importing it into the extension storage will fix this.\n\n\n"}
