{"step_index":169,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:55:30Z","content":"Here is why it looked like nothing happened:\n\nWhen you select the file in the Windows file picker and click \"Open\", **the file is just selected**. \n\nBecause your backup is heavily encrypted, you still need to complete the last 2 steps in that popup box on your screen:\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step:\n1. Click **\"📂 Import Localhost Backup\"** again.\n2. Select your `.json` backup file and click **Open**.\n3. Look at the box right below it: **type your Master Password** (the password you used in the localhost app).\n4. Click the blue **\"⚡ Decrypt & Import\"** button!\n\nAs soon as you click **\"⚡ Decrypt & Import\"**, it will decrypt your file and you will see:\n> `🎉 Success! Imported 2 credentials into your extension!`\n\n---\n\n### Or the fastest way (10 seconds):\nIf you don't want to use files, you can also just save it directly into the extension right now:\n1. In the extension popup on `vitvellore312.examly.io`, click the green **`＋ Add`** button at the top.\n2. Type:\n   - **Username**: `vijay.rohra2025@vitstudent...`\n   - **Password**: your password\n3. Click **\"Save to Vault\"**.\n\nOnce saved, it will stay in the extension permanently and auto-fill every time!"}
